RECALL (D108): the sweep showed transient below-floor dips that never consolidate.
If r~0 here, that non-consolidation IS a heritability failure (selectionist) -> the fix is
about making variation transmit (e.g. the reverberation/structure-copying angle, S2), not
about more selection pressure. If r>0, heritability is fine and the density-activity
hypothesis (too much activity -> poor differentiation) is the live lead.
